// The stale-mask/ARM-INIT interaction (aug08b ryouko
// reactive/000000, the stale mask's SECOND regression after
// dyncall-loop-stale-ride): a BECOMING-SELECTED arm updates under the
// interp's init view — everything re-delivers as an ARRIVAL and
// CachedArgs re-evals — but the kernel's stale mask read the RAW
// input discs, so the re-selected arm's first dispatch delivered its
// quiet inputs as STALE and the site surfaced its LAST RESULT from a
// previous selection (a list::to_array returned the pre-deselection
// array; the interp re-eval'd fresh).
//
// Reduced witness (probe p2):
//   { let v0 = select i64:0 { _ if in0 => list::to_array(list::map(
//       list::from_array(["a", "a"]), |x| in1)), in0 => [i64:0, i64:1] };
//     v0[i64:-1]$ }
//   epochs in0=t; in0=f in1=1; in0=t  ->  interp 1,0,1,1  jit 1,0,1,0
//
// Fix history: aug08b suppressed the emitted stale mask under the
// EFFECTIVE init view (arm override included) — everything fired at
// arm wake, eval re-ran, matching the interp's then arrival
// semantics. The present-but-stale commits (9b2e7231, 2026-08-31)
// moved the interp and this pin diverged with the engines SWAPPED
// (interp rode, jit recomputed). RE-ADJUDICATED under WAKE CATCH-UP
// (design/wake_catchup.md, Eric 2026-09-01): the trace is
// 1, 0, 1, 1 on BOTH engines, by the ruled mechanism — in1's fire is
// HELD (the selected `[0,1]` arm doesn't read it), and the map arm's
// wake consumes it as a genuine catch-up fire; the forced recompute
// covers the value plane. The stale mask now suppresses only under
// GENUINE init (wire bit 0 & !bit 2 — the wake bit).
// schedule-v1: cap=208 events=1664; in0=bool:true; in0=bool:false in1=i64:1; in0=bool:true
{let v1: i64 = {let v0 = select i64:0 {_ if in0 => list::to_array(list::map(list::from_array(["a", "a"]), |v0| in1)), in0 => [i64:0, (i64:-100 - i64:7)]}; select in0 {v1 if (f64:3.14 >= f64:2.5) => v0[i64:-1]$, in1 => cast<i64>((-(z64:-1)))$}}; let v2 = i64:0; v2 <- in0 ~ (select in0 {true => v2 + i64:1, false => v2}); ((v2 + v2) * v1)}
